# Low Water, Act 1: evidence and shared flags. Director's file.
# Evidence has about (the Daybook line), against (who and weight) and by (how it was read).
# against ids: keel, crake (the Trust and Board's side as trust), trust, guild, wenna, sabine,
# fennick, merrow. The dawn verdict reads these weights.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- evidence: the bible's clues C1 to C16
@fact prints.read
about: Boot prints, size eleven, from the steps to the drowned lamp after the floor opened; deeper heels coming back.
against: merrow 10
by: eyes

@fact scales.switch
about: Fish scales on the handle of the quay switch box, under the eave.
against: guild 20
by: eyes, in light

@fact works.order
about: The works order: Mother moved from her own feeder onto the quay board seven months ago. Signed Keel, approved Crake.
against: keel 25
against: trust 30
by: reading

@fact panel.restrike
about: The card on Mother's panel: RESTRIKE REQUIRED after any loss of supply. A keeper's job.
against: trust 20
against: wenna 10
by: reading

@fact log.ahead
about: The lamp-room log is filled in to the end of the month, in ink all of one age.
against: wenna 15
by: reading and the Damp

@fact coat.wenna_dry
about: Wenna's oilskin is dry. Nobody who walked the mole tonight is dry.
against: wenna 15
by: the Damp

@fact tab.wenna
about: The Brine's tab: rounds in Wenna's mark at 21:45 and 22:10, by the Brine's own slow clock.
against: wenna 10
against: sabine 5
by: reading

@fact prism.green_oven
about: A prism of green bottle glass, still warm, in the Brine's bread oven.
against: wenna 20
against: sabine 15
by: Candlemas, out of the sodium

@fact lens.green
about: A third of Mother's prism rings are green bottle glass. Her beam is green and weak.
against: wenna 20
by: Candlemas, in the arc's light or by lantern

@fact prism.numbered
about: Fennick's relic: a sharp-edged crown glass prism, numbered 113 on its edge. Not sea glass. One of Mother's.
against: wenna 10
against: fennick 15
by: Candlemas, in the dark

@fact overheard.last_three
about: Sabine to Wenna in the yard: that was the last three, and she would not fire the oven for glass again.
against: wenna 10
against: sabine 10
by: overhearing

@fact merrow.wet_thigh
about: Merrow is wet to the thigh: he waded the gully late, when it was deep.
against: merrow 5
by: the Damp

@fact memory.low_light
about: From the ferry's deck: a low light in the drowned lamp, 22:24 by the ship's clock, and the helm going over.
by: memory

@fact claim.time
about: The Board's claim was telegraphed at 18:30, three hours before the dark.
against: keel 30
by: reading

@fact lamps.pink
about: The quay lamps came back pink. Sodium restarts through red for about ten minutes, so the quay was dark until about 21:52.
against: guild 10
by: testimony and Candlemas

@fact soot.east
about: Soot streaked east across the weigh-house's east face: the Brine's oven ran while the wind was still west, before 23:35.
against: sabine 10
by: the Vane and the Damp

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- further evidence
@fact marrow.switch
about: Marrow pulled the quay switch at 21:38 for the vote, as the Guild has for thirty years, and put it back at 21:52. He did not know Mother was on it.
against: guild 25
by: testimony

@fact merrow.light
about: Merrow hung a lantern in the drowned lamp's hole tonight. He says it went out at 22:18 and burned again from 22:25.
by: testimony

@fact spray.mole
about: The mole has been spray-swept in a westerly since nine. Anyone who walked it is wet on the windward side.
by: the Vane

@fact key.office
about: Keel's key to the weigh-house office.
by: Keel

@fact wenna.heard_motor
about: Wenna heard Mother's motor stop at twenty to ten, from her seat by the Brine's stove, and did not go.
against: wenna 25
by: testimony

@fact sabine.oven
about: Sabine casts the green prisms in the bread oven from the Brine's empties, on bread nights. Six years of it.
against: sabine 25
against: wenna 15
by: testimony

@fact fennick.bought
about: Fennick paid Wenna for the splinters of the Eye, in coin and silence, for six years.
against: fennick 25
against: wenna 15
by: testimony

@fact clause.struck
about: The engineer's specification: the clause requiring a keeper to restrike Mother after any loss of supply, struck through in yellow ink. Readable only out of the sodium.
against: trust 30
by: reading, in honest light

@fact frost.keel
about: Frozen drips on the hundred and twelve stairs, one per step, going up and coming down. Keel climbed to Mother before dawn.
against: keel 20
by: the frost

@fact hammer.keel
about: Constant Hobb saw the harbourmaster take the lump hammer from the weigh-house store at a quarter past four.
against: keel 15
by: testimony

@fact vote.older
about: One of the two fish on the Guild's voting pans was smoked a day before the vote.
against: guild 5
by: SMELL and Shadwell's soot

@fact ship.clock
about: The Saint Cuthwin's clock runs four minutes fast. The ferry turned at 22:20 by the true time.
by: Penhallow

@fact brine.clock
about: The Brine's clock is eleven minutes slow. Sabine corrects it for everyone but herself.
against: sabine 5
by: SUM

@fact lens.keel_motive
about: Keel wants a whole new lens at the Shelf's expense, so that nobody counts the green rings.
against: keel 20
by: testimony or inference

@fact pollard.file
about: The Shelf's own file on Mother's conversion, twelve years ago, assessed by H. Pollard. He passed the lens as whole.
by: reading

@fact shelf.e
about: The Shelf's messages are typed on a machine with a sticking e.
by: SMALL PRINT

